From 889c7867c01cab01b371c5fb28c62b61186ddc7e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 07:50:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Ease-of-use audit "do first" items 1, 2, 5, 6, 7 and 8

1. What was untrue: "What asks first" now says web search asks only when
   something private could slip in (every time only with "Ask before every
   web search" on), and lists "Read your calendar" once; About and the FAQ
   no longer say every action asks; deep answers last until Jarvis stops;
   History says when an answer was not kept; the phone's refusal names only
   the .ts.net/.nord names it can reach; the FAQ, INSTALL 3.4, 2.5 and the
   log notes match today's messages and places.
2. "Jarvis isn't running" names the real Start button, and the desktop
   adds "Show me where" (Settings, More options, open); the autostart
   switch says it starts Jarvis Desktop; "Let my phone reach this" says it
   needs the app to start Jarvis.
5. One wording pass: Connected, Catching up..., Model, Background jobs,
   Jarvis bar, Pause background learning, Settings and help..., Faces
   retitled and its untrue sentence fixed; "State of mind" and "route
   badge" dropped.
6. Error details are selectable in both apps (no Copy button).
7. History dates show the weekday; Delete says facts are not forgotten;
   a filter box on "What Jarvis knows about you" (desktop).
8. README and INSTALL: the real preflight line, the backend is not
   public, Tailscale steps, keep the PC awake (plus a preflight WARN),
   updating everything, a lost phone, all seven Credential Manager
   entries; selftest stops with one message in the wrong folder; the
   patch script keeps a log of each run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015UUeD3W4kG7RWyUe7qR4bc
